{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Surface\nAWS CloudWatch, us-east-1, acct 896586841071, host `rebar-gerrit`. Three correlated autodeploy alarms flapped 2026-08-29→30: `deploy_errors` ×11, `mcp_retire_cap` ×11, `review_interrupts_signal_unavailable` ×2. Deploy path is fail-safe (no outage) but releases were not landing cleanly and in-flight reviews may have been killed blind. Full RCA + evidence is in this ticket's RCA comment.\n\n## Root cause (proven — detail in the RCA comment)\n**Mechanism 1 (deploy_errors ×11 + mcp-retire-cap ×11, one event).** `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` sets uvicorn `timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(grace_seconds)` (line 743) with `grace_seconds` defaulting to the 1200s certified-op drain budget `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` (line 51), and `make_sigterm_handler` sets `server.should_exit=True` **before** draining the in-flight gauge. Streamable-HTTP clients hold long-lived streams, so uvicorn's graceful shutdown waits the full 1200s for idle held-open streams even at 0 in-flight. With only two blue-green ports a retiring container pins a port ~20 min → the next mcp deploy hits `port-exhausted` → `deploy_failed` + backoff. A landing burst drove it 11×.\n\n**Mechanism 3 (signal-unavailable ×2).** In `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` the drain gate reads the bot `/health` `in_flight`; on an unreadable signal `bot_in_flight_reviews()` returns `-1` and the gate **fails open** — recreates the bot with no drain check, emitting `AUTODEPLOY_REVIEW_INTERRUPT signal-unavailable`. It cannot tell a bot that is **mid-redeploy** (unreachable only because it is being recreated / still starting) from one genuinely **wedged**; the blind recreate can kill the very startup it should wait for.\n\n## Approach\nTwo independent, bounded, reversible fixes; each with its own RED→GREEN test.\n\n**Fix 1 — decouple uvicorn graceful-shutdown from the certified-op grace (`_mcp_health.py`).**\n- Add a short constant `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS` for `uvicorn.Config(timeout_graceful_shutdown=...)`, decoupled from `grace_seconds` (which stays the op-drain budget); thread it as a defaulted `uvicorn_graceful_seconds` param on `run_http_with_grace` for testability.\n- Reorder `make_sigterm_handler._on_sigterm` to drain the gauge FIRST (existing `drain_then_exit`, bounded by `grace_seconds`) and set `server.should_exit=True` only AFTER the gauge hits 0. A real in-flight op's streaming response then completes normally; once the gauge is 0, uvicorn's short backstop sweeps idle held-open streams in seconds instead of the full 1200s.\n- Close NEW intake at SIGTERM so the fast-drain-at-0 cannot be re-pinned by a landing burst: add a `draining` flag to `InFlightGauge` (`begin_draining()`), and have the certified-op wrapper REFUSE a new certified op (raise `MCPRetiringError`, never incrementing) once draining. `_on_sigterm` calls `begin_draining()` FIRST (immediate intake-stop), before the drain loop; a certified request arriving mid-drain is rejected so the client retries the live (green) container and the gauge can actually reach 0. (uvicorn's `should_exit`-first intake-stop cannot be reused: with a short `timeout_graceful_shutdown` it would force-close a real in-flight op.) Ops already counted still drain to completion.\n- Invariant preserved: >0 in-flight ⇒ full `grace_seconds` drain (never cut a real op short); 0 in-flight ⇒ fast drain; new intake refused during drain ⇒ a burst cannot extend the window or re-pin the port. The op bound is enforced by the gauge poll, never uvicorn's short backstop.\n\n**Fix 3 — distinguish \"bot mid-redeploy\" from \"bot wedged\" (`autodeploy.sh`).**\n- Add best-effort `bot_unreachable_disposition()` inspecting the bot container's docker state/health → `redeploying` (status `restarting`/`created`/`removing`/`paused`, or health `starting`) vs `wedged` (running-but-unreachable, `unhealthy`, no container, or any inspect error → default `wedged`).\n- In the drain gate's `inflight < 0` branch, when `redeploying`, DEFER (retry next tick) with a countable `AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED bot-redeploying` marker, bounded by the existing `DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX` episode; on bound-exhaustion or `wedged`, fall through to the existing fail-open recreate + `signal-unavailable`. Maps the single unknown `-1` onto its own disposition instead of a blind fail-open (mirrors the 1c0d disposition-contract intent).\n- Invariant preserved: a wedged/down bot still fails open and deploys (recovery path); the mid-redeploy defer is bounded so it cannot live-lock the gate; any docker error defaults to `wedged` (pre-fix behavior).\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — Fix 1 only. No change to `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` (stays 1200), the gauge, or `drain_then_exit`.\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` — Fix 3 only. No change to the `inflight > 0` busy-defer path, the port pool, or `MCP_RELEASES_CAP`.\n- Tests otherwise. **Deferred / out of scope:** raising `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` / expanding the port pool (Option 2); any nginx/compose capacity change; the concurrent disk bug e4f3.\n\n## Testing\n- Fix 1 (`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py`): the pre-existing `test_make_sigterm_handler_stops_intake_then_drains` (asserting the OLD `should_exit`-first ordering Fix 1 reverses) is REWRITTEN — not kept green — into `..._drains_gauge_before_stopping_intake_2f46`, asserting `should_exit` stays False while the gauge is >0 and flips only after it hits 0 (fast-drain + >0-in-flight guard); the `installs_sigterm_and_bounds` test's `timeout_graceful_shutdown` assertion is updated from `== 1200` to `== DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS`. New tests: decoupled `timeout_graceful_shutdown` (< 1200s grace); and a new certified op during draining refused (`MCPRetiringError`) without incrementing the gauge. Other `run_http_with_grace` callers (startup-handshake / opcert / tool-offload) assert no such ordering and are unaffected.\n- Fix 3 (`tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py`, real-bash stub harness): mid-redeploy bot (unreachable `/health` + docker `starting`/`restarting`) is DEFERRED (no `compose build/up`, `AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED bot-redeploying`, no `signal-unavailable`, deployed-sha unchanged, rc 0); wedged bot (unreachable + docker `running`) still fails open (`compose build` runs, `signal-unavailable` counted); the mid-redeploy defer is bounded (`DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX=0` falls through to fail-open).\n- `make lint` + `make typecheck` + the two test modules; mutation check with teeth on the changed logic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A retiring MCP container with 0 in-flight certified ops shuts down within the short `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS` backstop (not the 1200s op grace), proven by a test asserting `timeout_graceful_shutdown == DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS < DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS`.\n- [ ] A retiring MCP container with >0 in-flight certified ops still receives the full `grace_seconds` drain and is never cut short, proven by a test asserting `should_exit` stays False until the gauge reaches 0.\n- [ ] A NEW certified op arriving after SIGTERM (during the drain) is REFUSED (`MCPRetiringError`) and does not increment the gauge, while an already-in-flight op is unaffected — so a burst cannot re-pin the retiring port for the full grace. Proven by a gauge-level and a handler-level test.\n- [ ] An unreadable `/health` caused by a mid-redeploy bot yields a DEFER with a countable `AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED bot-redeploying` marker and no `compose build/up`, asserted by the bash harness.\n- [ ] A genuinely wedged/down bot (or an exhausted mid-redeploy defer bound) still fails open, runs `compose build`, and emits the countable `AUTODEPLOY_REVIEW_INTERRUPT signal-unavailable` marker, asserted by the bash harness.\n- [ ] No capacity change is made: `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` and the blue-green port set are unchanged; both fixes are in-process/host-local with no CI-provider dependency.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the two targeted test modules pass; each mechanism has an independent RED→GREEN test."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788147749792498703,"uuid":"aaf45572-d6b2-4fc2-81e1-b3db7220b2a8"}